==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[directed]] [[graph]]}}

# {{context|graph theory|lang=en}} A [[graph]] in which the [[edge]]s are [[ordered pair]]s, so that, if the edge (a, b) is in the graph, the edge (b, a) need not be in the graph and is distinct from (a, b) if it is.
#: A '''directed graph''' (''A'',''R'') is a set of vertices ''A'' together with an incidence relation ''R'': if ''aRb'' then there is an edge going from ''A'' to ''B''.

====Antonyms====
* [[undirected graph]]

====Synonyms====
* [[digraph]]

